  <content>
    <section>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
        <item>Desmos activity: Exponential Graph Maps</item>
      </list>
      <div class="os-raise-usermessage-link">
        <para>Log into <link url="https://student.desmos.com">student.desmos.com</link> using the information provided by your teacher to complete the activity.</para>
      </div>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
        <item>Functions \(f\) and \(g\)<emphasis> </emphasis>are defined by these equations: </item>
      </list>
      <list>
        <item>\(f(x)=1,000 \cdot (\frac{1}{10})^x\)</item>
        <item>\(g(x)=1,000 \cdot (\frac{9}{10})^x\)</item>
      </list>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
          <item>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. On the same coordinate plane, sketch a graph that represents the functions, \(f\) and \(g\). It may be helpful to use a different color for each function. </item>
        </list>
      </list>
      <div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-bottom="0" data-left="0" data-right="1200" data-schema-version="1.0" data-top="25"/>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answers:</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_14_06_01.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
            </para>
          </solution>
